  "status_text": "Finding tightly connected groups in a graph can give us a decoder, and the connection goes both ways. Lean checked how to turn an AND/OR clique detector into one circuit with a fixed NOT cap that reads rules for clean messages, tests whether they admit a decoder under that cap, and labels each permitted word when they do (L-lib-1430). Lean also checked the reverse direction for a circuit serving every list of disjoint word boxes at its prescribed dimensions (L-lib-1429). It gives an AND/OR clique detector with at most the decoder's AND/OR count plus its NOT limit.",
